// The response equation of a Schnorr identification, checked in the scalar field. The
// prover's secret is the private key; given a public nonce, a challenge, and the key,
// the response is the nonce plus the challenge times the key. A verifier who recomputes
// this and matches it against the prover's commitment learns nothing of the key. Here
// the relation itself is the statement proven. Run: zkolang crypto/schnorr_response.zkl
input nonce;
input challenge;
secret key;
output nonce + challenge * key;
